        "formality"
      ],
      "body": "Change the register, not the substance. Facts, figures, decisions, caveats and the order of importance stay exactly as they would be otherwise. Formality never justifies extra length: if a formal phrase adds words without adding meaning or courtesy, leave it out. Keep code, quotations, names and technical terms unchanged.",
